      "description": "Watch Neom SC vs Al Fayha highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 14, 2026. The Pro League returned to action with a highly anticipated fixture on 2026-08-14 as Neom SC squared off against Al Fayha . Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish momentum in a match that promised tactical depth and individual brilliance. Clinical Finishing Defines the Opening Half Neom SC wasted little time asserting their authority on home soil. The breakthrough arrived in the 26th minute when Said Benrahma turned provider, setting up Amadou Kone for a composed finish to break the deadlock. The pressure remained relentless, and despite an early tactical change that saw Nawaf Al Harthi replace Jason , the hosts doubled their advantage in the 36th minute. This time, Alexandre Lacazette delivered a precise assist for Said Benrahma , who capped off a brilliant team move to send the hosts into the break with a commanding lead. Discipline Issues and the Final Blow The second half took a dramatic turn in the 62nd minute when Alaa Hajji was shown a straight red card. The decision sparked heavy protests from the Al Fayha players, but the referee remained firm, leaving the visitors with a mountain to climb. Capitalizing on the extra man, Neom SC found their third goal in the 76th minute as Hugo Moura found the back of the net following an assist from Nawaf Al Harthi . Amidst a flurry of late substitutions and a yellow card for Silvere Ganvoula , the hosts maintained total control until the final whistle at 90+7', securing a comprehensive 3-0 victory."
